# CUPID-CJPL custom macro command reference
#
# Reference only: every example is commented out. Executing this file performs
# no actions. Copy the commands you need into a separate run macro.
# This reference stays in the source macros/ directory; it is not a run preset.
#
# Scope: application-defined /cupid/ commands only. Geant4-native /run/, /gun/,
# /random/, /control/, /tracking/ and /vis/ commands are not project commands.
# Names and candidate values are case sensitive. Angle brackets indicate a
# required argument; square brackets indicate an optional argument. Do not
# copy those brackets into an actual command.
#
# States:
#   PreInit: before /run/initialize.
#   Idle: after /run/initialize, before /run/beamOn, or between completed runs.
# No command below is available while events are being processed.
# Initial settings below apply before any user macro overrides them; a required
# argument cannot be omitted just because an initial setting is documented.
# All custom commands execute on the master/serial UI, without worker broadcast.
#
# Maintenance: update this file whenever a custom command is added, renamed,
# removed, or changes parameters, units, defaults, allowed states or behavior.
# Keep the reference consistent with the command registration and its handler.

# ============================================================================
# Geometry -- src/geometry/GeometryMessenger.cc
# ============================================================================

# Command: /cupid/geometry/enable <component>
# Purpose: include a component in the next initial geometry construction.
# Argument: Cryostat, InnerShielding or LMOArray (required).
# State: PreInit.
# Initial setting: all three components are disabled; World is built separately.
# This selects an existing component; it does not create a new component type.
# Example:
# /cupid/geometry/enable LMOArray

# Command: /cupid/geometry/disable <component>
# Purpose: exclude a component from the initial geometry construction.
# Argument: Cryostat, InnerShielding or LMOArray (required).
# State: PreInit.
# Does not remove geometry after initialization. Restart with a different macro
# to change component selection once geometry has been initialized.
# Example:
# /cupid/geometry/disable InnerShielding

# Command: /cupid/geometry/list
# Purpose: print component enable/disable settings and the configured LMO count.
# Arguments: none.
# States: PreInit, Idle.
# Reports configuration, not a full list of physical volumes or an overlap check.
# Example:
# /cupid/geometry/list

# Command: /cupid/geometry/lmoCount <count>
# Purpose: configure the number of LMO crystals in LMOArray.
# Argument: integer 1 or 2 (required, dimensionless).
# State: PreInit. Initial setting: 1.
# One crystal is centered; two are arranged along X. This command does not
# enable LMOArray. Use /cupid/geometry/enable LMOArray separately.
# Example:
# /cupid/geometry/lmoCount 2

# Command: /cupid/geometry/check [samples]
# Purpose: check placed non-World volumes for overlaps using Geant4 checks.
# Argument: integer >= 100, optional; default when omitted: 10000.
# State: Idle.
# samples is the number of random surface probes per placed volume, not the
# number of simulated events. An overlap causes command failure. A sampled
# PASS is not a mathematical proof that every overlap is absent.
# Examples (equivalent sample counts):
# /cupid/geometry/check
# /cupid/geometry/check 10000

# ============================================================================
# Generator -- src/generator/GeneratorMessenger.cc
# ============================================================================

# Command: /cupid/generator/select <source>
# Purpose: select an implemented primary-generation path.
# Argument: gun (the only supported value; required).
# State: PreInit. Initial setting: gun.
# Configure the native particle gun with /gun/ commands after initialization.
# Dedicated calibration/background/double-beta generators are not selectable
# yet. This command does not select a position sampler.
# Example:
# /cupid/generator/select gun

# Command: /cupid/generator/verbose <level>
# Purpose: enable or suppress the project primary-particle diagnostic line.
# Argument: integer 0 or 1 (required, dimensionless).
# State: PreInit. Initial setting: 0.
# 0: suppress this diagnostic. 1: print one line per generated event, describing
# its first primary particle. Use 1 for small debugging runs only. This does
# not change Geant4 tracking/run verbosity or the physical source distribution.
# Example:
# /cupid/generator/verbose 1

# Command: /cupid/generator/list
# Purpose: print the selected generator and its configuration entry point.
# Arguments: none.
# States: PreInit, Idle.
# Currently reports the gun selection and /gun/ configuration prefix.
# Example:
# /cupid/generator/list

# Command: /cupid/generator/check
# Purpose: verify that the selected generator name is supported.
# Arguments: none.
# State: Idle.
# A PASS validates selection only, not gun position, nuclide data, transport,
# decay physics or the suitability of a source model for an experiment.
# Example:
# /cupid/generator/check

# ============================================================================
# Output -- src/output/OutputMessenger.cc (native G4GenericMessenger properties)
# RunAction owns the settings and applies them when each run starts.
# ============================================================================

# Command: /cupid/output/fileName <prefix>
# Purpose: set the shared filename prefix for subsequent runs.
# Argument: auto, or a custom prefix with an optional trailing .root (required).
# State: Idle. Initial setting: auto. Persists until changed.
# auto uses process-local time: runYYYYMMDD_HHMMSS (seconds, no microseconds).
# A custom prefix starts with an ASCII letter/digit and contains only ASCII
# letters/digits, _, - or .; it cannot end in a dot or contain spaces/paths.
# The optional .root suffix is stripped before applying recorder suffixes.
# Names are validated and the run directory is reserved when the run starts.
# Existing names are skipped with _1, _2, ...; existing data are not overwritten.
# Output layout for prefix calibration with both recorders selected:
#   <parent>/calibration/calibration_EventEnergy.root
#   <parent>/calibration/calibration_IncidentEnergy.root
#   <parent>/calibration/run.log
# Empty recorder files may be removed; the run directory/log are retained.
# This command does not change the generator, recorders or output backend.
# Examples:
# /cupid/output/fileName calibration
# /cupid/output/fileName calibration.root
# /cupid/output/fileName auto

# Command: /cupid/output/directory <path>
# Purpose: set the parent output directory for subsequent runs.
# Argument: nonempty directory path (required); quote paths containing spaces.
# State: Idle. Initial setting: ./results/runs, or the startup --output value.
# Persists until changed. A macro setting overrides the startup --output value.
# Relative paths use the process working directory, not the macro directory.
# Use Linux paths in WSL (for example /home/... or /mnt/c/...). Missing parent
# directories are created at run start. Each run creates a separate child
# directory for its ROOT files and run.log; files are not placed loose here.
# Examples:
# /cupid/output/directory ./results/runs/calibration
# /cupid/output/directory ./results/tests/source-check
# /cupid/output/directory "./results/tests/source check"

# ============================================================================
# Configuration boundaries
# ============================================================================
# Position samplers are chosen inside concrete C++ generators, not by a custom
# macro command. Recorder selection is in EventAction::DefaultRecorders().
# Output backend selection is in ActionInitialization::CreateRunAction().
# Those C++ configuration changes require rebuilding the application.
#
# Order in a run macro:
#   1. Geometry selection/count and generator selection/verbosity (PreInit).
#   2. Native /run/initialize.
#   3. Geometry/generator checks, native /gun/ settings, output settings (Idle).
#   4. Native /run/beamOn N.
#   5. Optional source/output changes and another /run/beamOn N (Idle).
# Assistant-run tests must use ./results/tests/<task>/; production runs use
# ./results/runs/ or an explicitly selected production parent directory.
